	(property "Description" "TI MSPM0G3518-Q1 Arm Cortex-M0+ MCU, RHB (VQFN-32, 5x5mm body) package, orderable M0G3518QRHBRQ1 -- same die/part number as this build's MCU (MSPM0G3518_Q1_PM, REFERENCES.md [44]), on the smaller package option per docs/solutions/architecture-patterns/bom-creepage-audit-can485-faraday.md finding #1. RHB exposes only PA0-PA27 (no Port B/C); every pin below was re-derived pad-by-pad against that constraint, not renumbered from the PM map. See symbols/specs/MSPM0G3518_Q1_RHB.json for the full per-pin datasheet verification."
		(at 0 0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(hide yes)
		)
	)
	(property "Citation" "[44]"
		(at 0 0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(hide yes)
		)
	)
	(property "Verification" "VERIFIED against [44] (SLASFA6B) Figure 6-6 '32-pin RHB (0.5mm) (VQFN) Package Diagram' (p.14) and Table 6-2 'Pin Attributes' (pp.15-23, RHB column). Full per-pin pad/IOMUX-function citation and conflict check in symbols/specs/MSPM0G3518_Q1_RHB.json. PROVENANCE: this file replaces a prior generic, unwired symbol at this same path (generator tag 'serenity_cleanroom_2026_08_03') that was authored for an unrelated board and internally named after that board's character call-sign; the name is scrubbed here per this repository's own no-cross-project-naming-leak hygiene, and every claim it made (package, footprint, pinout) was independently re-verified against [44] before reuse rather than carried over on trust. A DEFECT in that prior file was found and fixed: it declared 33 pins, including a spurious duplicate 'VSS' at pin '33' -- RHB is a real 32-pin package and has no such pin; it is not reproduced here. PIN COORDINATES are intentionally IDENTICAL to symbols/MSPM0G3518_Q1_PM.kicad_sym's corresponding named pin (same local (at x y rotation), same electrical type, same functional-role name) so that swapping U1 from the PM symbol to this one in builds/6s/50A/CAN_485_faraday leaves existing wires connected without moving them -- only the physical pin NUMBER changes, to its RHB equivalent. Verified by re-running kicad-cli sch erc after the swap: 0 errors, same warning set as before the swap (see the build's own ERC history)."
		(at 0 0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(hide yes)
		)
	)
